1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,450
NOBODY is hacking anything!

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:03,982
Too late.

3
00:00:31,082 --> 00:00:34,951
Okay, team! Listen up! We have a major situation.

4
00:00:35,701 --> 00:00:40,771
Mom and Dad left us in charge for two hours, which means we need absolute order.

5
00:00:42,271 --> 00:00:48,286
Abdel-Hamid, stop eating that for five seconds and sit up! You're going to get crumbs in the server rack!

6
00:00:49,435 --> 00:00:53,901
Aziza, relax. Entropy is a natural law of the universe.

7
00:00:54,651 --> 00:01:02,537
Me dropping paprika flakes on the carpet is just thermodynamic equilibrium. Besides, my energy level is currently at an optimal... zero.

8
00:01:03,787 --> 00:01:10,721
Her heart rate is elevated. She's going to forget why she's mad in roughly forty seconds. Watch.

9
00:01:11,671 --> 00:01:18,944
I heard that, Hicham! And give me that phone right now! Four-year-olds do not need to study quantum encryption algorithms!

10
00:01:19,894 --> 00:01:25,486
Negative. The algorithm feed is optimal. You're just jealous my screen time is higher than your grades.

11
00:01:26,637 --> 00:01:30,843
That's it! Where is Amir? He was supposed to help me secure the perimeter!

12
00:01:36,543 --> 00:01:41,840
GOAL! Unstoppable! What a strike by the tactical genius of the century!

13
00:01:42,490 --> 00:01:45,001
Aziza, clear the midfield, I'm running drills!

14
00:01:48,001 --> 00:01:55,314
You nearly disrupted my calculations with your kinetic nonsense, Amir. Go kick your ball outside. Preferably in another postal code.

15
00:01:56,364 --> 00:01:59,879
Look, ancient philosopher, stop acting like you're too old to move.

16
00:02:00,528 --> 00:02:08,129
I've already calculated the trajectory of your snack bag, and if you don't hand over a chip right now, I'm executing a tactical slide tackle on your chair.

17
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:13,519
And don't treat me like a kid! I play for a competitive youth club. I know pressure!

18
00:02:15,618 --> 00:02:17,276
Stop it! Both of you!

19
00:02:17,925 --> 00:02:25,554
Amir, stop playing football inside the house before you break the TV! And Abdel-Hamid, get up! We have a schedule!

20
00:02:26,403 --> 00:02:31,798
Step one: clean the living room. Step two: homework. Step three...

21
00:02:33,348 --> 00:02:35,361
wait. What was step three again?

22
00:02:37,662 --> 00:02:42,936
Ugh, it was right on the tip of my tongue... something important about the kitchen timer...

23
00:02:44,086 --> 00:02:48,304
See? Total memory failure. This is why I should be the group leader.

24
00:02:48,954 --> 00:02:53,343
My reaction time is zero point two seconds, and my mental database never lags.

25
00:02:54,294 --> 00:02:58,395
You are seven years old, Amir! You are not leading anything!

26
00:03:03,395 --> 00:03:04,954
Houston, we have a breach.

27
00:03:05,704 --> 00:03:10,707
The automated script I wrote to bypass the Wi-Fi parental lock has triggered a system feedback loop.

28
00:03:12,307 --> 00:03:15,752
You did WHAT?! Hicham, give me that phone right now!

29
00:03:16,902 --> 00:03:19,586
Negative. You lack the necessary clearance, Aziza.

30
00:03:20,235 --> 00:03:26,560
If I don't re-route the local network within thirty seconds, all the smart lights in the house are going to start flashing Morse code.

31
00:03:27,909 --> 00:03:29,622
Incredible.

32
00:03:30,372 --> 00:03:35,917
A four-year-old just launched a cyber-attack on our own house because he wanted uninterrupted video time.

33
00:03:36,667 --> 00:03:42,002
Hand it here, Hicham. Let the master handle it, before Mom gets home and grounds us into the next geological epoch.

34
00:03:43,051 --> 00:03:48,542
Wait, let me hack it! I have lightning-fast reflexes! I can tap the screen a hundred times a second!

35
00:03:49,491 --> 00:03:52,817
Nobody is hacking anything! Give me the device!

36
00:04:09,717 --> 00:04:12,480
My... my skyscraper grid...

37
00:04:14,031 --> 00:04:21,682
Oh no... Amir, I am so, so sorry! I completely forgot the Lego layout was there! My memory just slipped...

38
00:04:23,033 --> 00:04:25,156
It's... it's fine. Whatever.

39
00:04:26,007 --> 00:04:31,607
A true tactician always accounts for structural collapse. We just rebuild it. Better. Stronger.

40
00:04:32,357 --> 00:04:33,901
With defensive turrets!

41
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:41,976
Here. Put this load-bearing beam in the center. Your first design had a structural flaw anyway.

42
00:04:57,776 --> 00:05:03,271
And look... I patched the Wi-Fi exploit. The house is saved from digital doom.

43
00:05:04,021 --> 00:05:07,060
Can I go back to my equations now? My brain needs calories.

44
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:14,877
Okay. Crisis averted. Total chaos... but averted.

45
00:05:15,726 --> 00:05:22,774
Everyone back in your spots before Mom pulls into the driveway! Amir, pick up those bricks. Hicham, no more code-breaking today.

46
00:05:23,524 --> 00:05:26,612
And Abdel-Hamid... please wipe the chip dust off your shirt.

47
00:05:40,612 --> 00:05:42,848
Welcome to the M'Rani Family channel!

48
00:05:43,499 --> 00:05:51,870
Tune in next time, because keeping a genius toddler, a football-obsessed troublemaker, and a lazy couch philosopher alive is an extreme sport...

49
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:55,132
wait, what was I about to say next?

50
00:05:56,081 --> 00:05:58,850
Ah, whatever! Don't forget to like and subscribe!

51
00:05:59,949 --> 00:06:03,134
And remember, I'm the real brains of the operation!

52
00:06:04,184 --> 00:06:04,771
False.

